el to further divide the sequences into basic paragraphs"], "model_visible_form_verbatim": "Chromosome 1 DNA sequence segments", "carrier_family": "discrete_biological_symbol_stream", "carrier_subtype": "native_biological_token_stream", "insertion_or_fusion_verbatim": "segmentation model", "evidence_quote": "We first divided Chromosome 1 into 25 segments", "section_heading": "2.7. Genome Segmentation - Chapter Division - Sentence Splitting", "supporting_figure_or_table": "Figure 4. Structure of the Genome Catalog."}]}

