./data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/taxonomy/runs/discovery/shard_03/records/june_update_2026-06-10__rec_000350_23e4d9368797/june_update_2026_06_10_rec_000350_23e4d9368797_docling_json_20260812_141720/docling/document.dclg:1252:<![CDATA[Figure 1 plots the mean pair-wise JS divergence at each layer for baseline and v3. Baseline is nearly flat at JS ≈ 0 . 08-0 . 13 across layers, with a mild peak at layer 5. v3 more than doubles the JS in layers 10-22 (peak +0 . 17 at layer 12), tripling it relative to baseline (baseline L 12 = 0 . 082, v3 L 12 = 0 . 251). v3 also shows a secondary peak at the output layers ( L 28 = 0 . 287), reflecting a 'choose-the-modality-to-generate' function near lm_head .]]>  </text>
