./data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/taxonomy/runs/discovery/shard_02/records/full_2026-07-06__rec_003206_211e7d00b696/full_2026_07_06_rec_003206_211e7d00b696_docling_json_20260812_140520/docling/document.json:2036:      "orig": "Figure 1: Overview of the Cell2Sentence framework. Input single-cell data, including metadata, are converted into cell sentences for LLM fine-tuning. Inference, via prompting, generates new cell sentences that can be converted back to gene expression space.",
./data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/taxonomy/runs/discovery/shard_02/records/full_2026-07-06__rec_003206_211e7d00b696/full_2026_07_06_rec_003206_211e7d00b696_docling_json_20260812_140520/docling/document.json:2037:      "text": "Figure 1: Overview of the Cell2Sentence framework. Input single-cell data, including metadata, are converted into cell sentences for LLM fine-tuning. Inference, via prompting, generates new cell sentences that can be converted back to gene expression space."
./data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/taxonomy/runs/discovery/shard_02/records/full_2026-07-06__rec_003206_211e7d00b696/full_2026_07_06_rec_003206_211e7d00b696_docling_json_20260812_140520/docling/document.json:2895:      "orig": "To further corroborate the gene expression patterns of our generated cells, we employ gene expression heatmaps, presented in Figure 10. These heatmaps compare the differentially expressed genes for each cell type in both the generated and ground-truth cells, with the differential genes sourced from the top 100 genes in the ground truth dataset. The heatmaps confirm that the generated data is consistent with the overall structure in the original dataset while also highlighting subtle gene-level discrepancies. This enhances our understanding of how well the generated cells mimic the intricacies of the baseline data. Additionally, the analysis points to promising avenues for using generated cells to identify key marker genes, offering critical insights into cellular function and laying the groundwork for future research.",
./data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/taxonomy/runs/discovery/shard_02/records/full_2026-07-06__rec_003206_211e7d00b696/full_2026_07_06_rec_003206_211e7d00b696_docling_json_20260812_140520/docling/document.json:2896:      "text": "To further corroborate the gene expression patterns of our generated cells, we employ gene expression heatmaps, presented in Figure 10. These heatmaps compare the differentially expressed genes for each cell type in both the generated and ground-truth cells, with the differential genes sourced from the top 100 genes in the ground truth dataset. The heatmaps confirm that the generated data is consistent with the overall structure in the original dataset while also highlighting subtle gene-level discrepancies. This enhances our understanding of how well the generated cells mimic the intricacies of the baseline data. Additionally, the analysis points to promising avenues for using generated cells to identify key marker genes, offering critical insights into cellular function and laying the groundwork for future research."
./data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/taxonomy/runs/discovery/shard_02/records/full_2026-07-06__rec_003206_211e7d00b696/full_2026_07_06_rec_003206_211e7d00b696_docling_json_20260812_140520/docling/document.json:3085:      "orig": "Table 4 underscores the necessity of NL pretraining for accurate cell type identification. Figure 12 presents the corresponding confusion matrices. A significant performance decline is observed when using models that have not undergone NL pretraining, thereby confirming that the models are not merely memorizing the conditioning text. Despite 1) the limited scope of natural language text in our training prompts relative to the pretraining corpus, and 2) permitting the models to train on these natural language prompts, models without NL pretraining failed to acquire meaningful natural language embeddings. Furthermore, a modest performance increment is observed as the scale of pretrained models increases.",
./data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/taxonomy/runs/discovery/shard_02/records/full_2026-07-06__rec_003206_211e7d00b696/full_2026_07_06_rec_003206_211e7d00b696_docling_json_20260812_140520/docling/document.json:3086:      "text": "Table 4 underscores the necessity of NL pretraining for accurate cell type identification. Figure 12 presents the corresponding confusion matrices. A significant performance decline is observed when using models that have not undergone NL pretraining, thereby confirming that the models are not merely memorizing the conditioning text. Despite 1) the limited scope of natural language text in our training prompts relative to the pretraining corpus, and 2) permitting the models to train on these natural language prompts, models without NL pretraining failed to acquire meaningful natural language embeddings. Furthermore, a modest performance increment is observed as the scale of pretrained models increases."
./data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/taxonomy/runs/discovery/shard_02/records/full_2026-07-06__rec_003206_211e7d00b696/full_2026_07_06_rec_003206_211e7d00b696_docling_json_20260812_140520/docling/document.json:24502:      "orig": "Figure 10: Heatmap visualizations comparing differentially expressed genes per cell type between generated and ground truth expression data showing strong correspondence between generated and real cells across a number of cell types. Differentially expressed genes were identified from the top 100 genes in ground truth data.",
./data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/taxonomy/runs/discovery/shard_02/records/full_2026-07-06__rec_003206_211e7d00b696/full_2026_07_06_rec_003206_211e7d00b696_docling_json_20260812_140520/docling/document.json:24503:      "text": "Figure 10: Heatmap visualizations comparing differentially expressed genes per cell type between generated and ground truth expression data showing strong correspondence between generated and real cells across a number of cell types. Differentially expressed genes were identified from the top 100 genes in ground truth data."
./data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/taxonomy/runs/discovery/shard_02/records/full_2026-07-06__rec_003206_211e7d00b696/full_2026_07_06_rec_003206_211e7d00b696_docling_json_20260812_140520/docling/document.json:24583:      "orig": "Figure 11: Confusion matrices for KNN classification of cell types using 25 nearest neighbors. Models are (A) GPT-2 Small pretrained, (B) GPT-2 Small fine-tuned, (C) GPT-2 Medium pretrained, and (D) GPT-2 Medium fine-tuned. Fine-tuned models show clearer diagonal patterns, indicating better separation of cell types. This demonstrates improved generation fidelity from natural language pretraining and model scaling.",
./data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/taxonomy/runs/discovery/shard_02/records/full_2026-07-06__rec_003206_211e7d00b696/full_2026_07_06_rec_003206_211e7d00b696_docling_json_20260812_140520/docling/document.json:24584:      "text": "Figure 11: Confusion matrices for KNN classification of cell types using 25 nearest neighbors. Models are (A) GPT-2 Small pretrained, (B) GPT-2 Small fine-tuned, (C) GPT-2 Medium pretrained, and (D) GPT-2 Medium fine-tuned. Fine-tuned models show clearer diagonal patterns, indicating better separation of cell types. This demonstrates improved generation fidelity from natural language pretraining and model scaling."
./data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/taxonomy/runs/discovery/shard_02/records/full_2026-07-06__rec_003206_211e7d00b696/full_2026_07_06_rec_003206_211e7d00b696_docling_json_20260812_140520/docling/document.json:24664:      "orig": "Figure 12: Confusion matrices for autoregressive cell type prediction on unseen immune tissue test data. Models pretrained on natural language text before Cell2Sentence training (NL + C2S) significantly outperform models trained only on cell sentences (C2S). This demonstrates the benefits of transfer learning from natural language for predicting cell types from gene sequences.",
./data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/taxonomy/runs/discovery/shard_02/records/full_2026-07-06__rec_003206_211e7d00b696/full_2026_07_06_rec_003206_211e7d00b696_docling_json_20260812_140520/docling/document.json:24665:      "text": "Figure 12: Confusion matrices for autoregressive cell type prediction on unseen immune tissue test data. Models pretrained on natural language text before Cell2Sentence training (NL + C2S) significantly outperform models trained only on cell sentences (C2S). This demonstrates the benefits of transfer learning from natural language for predicting cell types from gene sequences."
./data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/taxonomy/runs/discovery/shard_02/records/full_2026-07-06__rec_003206_211e7d00b696/full_2026_07_06_rec_003206_211e7d00b696_docling_json_20260812_140520/docling/document.json:24745:      "orig": "Figure 13: UMAP plots comparing cell embeddings from C2S, scVI, and ground truth data. The Maximum Mean Discrepancy (MMD) statistic quantifies the difference in distributions. The lower MMDvalue for C2S indicates that our generated cells better match the real data distribution than the cells generated with scVI.",
./data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/taxonomy/runs/discovery/shard_02/records/full_2026-07-06__rec_003206_211e7d00b696/full_2026_07_06_rec_003206_211e7d00b696_docling_json_20260812_140520/docling/document.json:24746:      "text": "Figure 13: UMAP plots comparing cell embeddings from C2S, scVI, and ground truth data. The Maximum Mean Discrepancy (MMD) statistic quantifies the difference in distributions. The lower MMDvalue for C2S indicates that our generated cells better match the real data distribution than the cells generated with scVI."
./data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/taxonomy/runs/discovery/shard_02/records/full_2026-07-06__rec_003206_211e7d00b696/full_2026_07_06_rec_003206_211e7d00b696_docling_json_20260812_140520/docling/document.json:24772:      "orig": "Figure 14: UMAP visualization colored by cell type, comparing C2S, scVI, and ground truth data. Both C2S and scVI generate distinct cell types, but only C2S cells strongly align with ground truth cells of the matching type. This shows that the C2S framework can generate specific cell types that closely mimic real cells, outperforming scVI.",
